      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْصَرِفٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيْرُ مُنْصَرِفٍ</span> denote the two different
sorts of nouns, (O, K,) meaning, respectively,
[like ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَصْرُوفٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيْرُ مَصْرُوفٍ</span>,] <i>Inflected,</i> or
<i>declined, with tenween,</i> and <i>not so inflected</i> or
<i>declined.</i> (O, TA.)

